That doesn't have anything to do with Gehennom. When you think you have
everything you need, and if you intend to play for a quick ascension (I
usually don't, I play because I like the game), you should go ahead without
diversions. Wether that point is at the castle (completed AK with /WoW),
before it (maybe after a sacfest) or down in the mazes doesn't really
matter, does it? Why should it be _exactly_ at the end of the Valley?

